artifact at weight 0.6, so my confidence is capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02(2) — below the 0.70 floor — which independently triggers POL-RD-10(1).\n\nOn the rider's POL-RD-01 point: the numbers (4.0 km and 36.4% over the 11.0 km routing-engine optimal) do clear the 0.8 km and 20% establishment gates on the trace, but the trace is impaired, so the gate cannot be passed on the trace alone. The rider's POL-RD-02 arithmetic (charged 26.60; recomputed fare 20.831 using the fare_breakdown surge multiplier of 1.1; refund 5.77 rounded up to 5.80) is correct as far as it goes but is not reached, because the deviation it depends on is not established. The driver likewise has no exculpatory clause to invoke — the only traffic advisory is MISSING at weight 0.0, there is no pickup or dropoff amendment, no waypoint is resolved, and the vehicle type RYDE_X is not a pool — but that does not matter, because the rider's case cannot be proved on this record. The deviation is not MATERIAL (36.4% < 50%, 4.0 km < 8.0 km) and the driver shows no trailing-90-day pattern (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 610 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises; and every fare line is matched (erp_gantries empty, no airport surcharge), so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral arises.\n\nWhat the human reviewer needs to resolve this is a distance figure for the unobserved segment that does not depend on the broken trace — a platform-derived actual distance, a gantry record placing the vehicle off the booked corridor, or an admission — or a trace without the gap. Escalation is terminal: nothing is collected and nothing is refunded, and the disputed SGD 5.80 is held pending that review."
