e meter is derived from the same trace, so all three 15.0 km figures are one measurement, not three. POL-RD-07(iii) therefore applies: on this record the claim is neither proven nor disproven, and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because the missing proof is a data failure and not a finding for the driver.\n\nThis is also mandatory escalation under POL-RD-10(3), and separately under POL-RD-10(1): the fact that decides the case is carried only by EV-GPS-09115 at weight 0.6, so confidence is capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02(2), below the 0.70 platform floor that clause applies. The rider's POL-RD-08 initial burden likewise fails at element (b), because the trace is impaired and no POL-RD-07(ii) source stands in for it.\n\nON THE SURVIVING CLAIMS. The rider's POL-RD-01 arithmetic is accepted — 4.0 km and 36.36% over the 11.0 km routing-engine optimal clears both establishment gates, and gps_trace.trace_distance_km (15.0 km) is rightly used as the governing figure — but it does not decide the case, because a deviation cannot be established on this impaired, uncorroborated trace. The rider's POL-RD-02 computation is correct as arithmetic (charged_total 26.60, recomputed_fare 20.831, refund 5.769 rounded up to 5.80) but it does not run: POL-RD-02 operates only where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01, and here it is not. No refund of the 5.80 is ordered.\n\nThe driver's points are accepted. No exculpatory clause is available: the only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09115-01) is MISSING at weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot run; neither endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 cannot run; POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run because both chat messages carry waypoint_hint null and name no road, so that clause is unavailable; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The excess, though established on paper, is not MATERIAL (it is under 50% and under 8.0 km), and no POL-RD-06 pattern exists on the citable counters (deviation_flags_90d 0 over 610 completed trips in the trailing 90 days), so no driver-conduct referral and no FULL_REFUND uplift arise. No charge line is unmatched, so POL-RD-10(8) does not fire, and with erp_gantries empty and no airport surcharge there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. The referrals list is therefore empty.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT. A corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names — a driver admission in the chat log, a charged ERP gantry on an off-optimal corridor, a counterparty statement admitting the route, or an independently derived trip distance — or a continuous, repaired GPS trace covering 20:03:10 to 20:05:50. The reviewer is asked to obtain one of those before the disputed amount is settled either way."
