OL-RD-10(3) direct ESCALATE rather than a finding for either side - a data gap is a failure of proof, not a finding that the driver did nothing wrong. Independently, the only fact that could decide this case is carried by EV-GPS-09115 at weight 0.6, so confidence is capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02(2), below the platform-wide 0.70 floor that POL-RD-10(1) applies. ESCALATE is terminal and replaces any money ruling here.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CLAIMS. The arithmetic is correct: 4.0 km and 36.4% over the 11.0 km routing-engine optimal stored on the trip record clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and had the trace been sound the POL-RD-02 recomputation - charged_total 26.60, recomputed_fare 20.831 using the fare_breakdown surge_multiplier of 1.1, refund 5.769 rounded up to 5.80 - would have been payable. But the establishment cannot be made on an impaired, uncorroborated trace, so that refund does not issue on this record. The rider is also right that no exculpatory clause runs for the driver: EV-ADVIS-09115-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) so POL-RD-03 cannot run; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null so POL-RD-05 cannot run; both chat messages carry waypoint_hint null and name no road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test cannot be run and the clause is unavailable; and vehicle_type RYDE_X is not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. That removes any exoneration but does not supply the independent corroboration the rider needs.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CLAIMS. I accept that the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(b); that the impaired stretch reads as the 1.35 km straight line between bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver; that no POL-RD-07(ii) source exists; and that under POL-RD-08 the rider's initial burden is not discharged, so it never shifts. I also accept that this is not a MATERIAL deviation - 36.4% and 4.0 km fall short of the 50% and 8.0 km tests - and that no POL-RD-06 pattern exists (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 610 completed trips in the trailing 90 days, the only fields that clause permits), so there is no conduct referral and no remedy uplift against this driver. Escalation preserves the fare pending review; it is not a ruling in the driver's favour, and it refunds nothing to the rider.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT. A source of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names - a driver admission in the chat log, charged ERP gantries placing the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, a counterparty statement admitting the route, or a trip_record.actual_distance_km the platform derived independently of this trace - or a repaired trace covering 20:03 to 20:06. None is in the present record.",
